From: r00t <r00t@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] clipboard: include cstdint for the integer types
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

selection.h uses uint32_t and uint64_t but only got them through the
standard headers it includes. GCC 16's libstdc++ no longer includes
<cstdint> there, so the file failed to compile on Fedora 44.

--- a/src/clipboard/selection.h
+++ b/src/clipboard/selection.h
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 
 #pragma once
 
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <deque>
 #include <memory>
 #include <string>
